docs: add TODO.md so deferred work is written down, not remembered

Everything known-but-not-started now lives in one file, each item with
what the problem is, why it happens, what to do, and what to check first.

Four items:

1. The proxy needs to be started by hand while the shell starts only
   llama-server, so the settings panel often shows ECONNREFUSED and the
   QR falls back to 8091 where profiles do nothing. Plan is to have the
   shell manage it alongside the server, reusing the existing PID-ledger
   cleanup.

2. The QQ bridge is written and its Ed25519 verification matches the
   official example byte for byte, but it needs a public HTTPS callback.
   Both credential-free self-test modes still work.

3. Long single-shot generation degrades into repetition after roughly ten
   thousand tokens. Sampling was ruled out - five parameter sets, same
   degenerate prefix, all clean at 600 tokens. The variable is length, and
   chunked generation is the workaround that the evidence actually
   supports. The reproduce script used for that is one-off, so turning the
   degenerate text into a fixed regression fixture is still outstanding.

4. Placeholder addresses in the docs do not track network changes.

README's known-limitations list now points here for the last two.
